**BIOMAN**
The BIOMas of ANchovy (BIOMAN) survey series began in 1987 to improve the monitoring and assessment of the Bay of Biscay anchovy population. Initially, it aimed to estimate the total biomass of anchovy using the Daily Eggs Production Method (DEPM). Over time, the survey expanded to include other pelagic species like sardine, mackerel, and horse mackerel.Currently, BIOMAN follows an integrated ecosystem approach, aligning with the European Marine Strategy Framework Directive and the Common Fisheries Policy. The survey’s objectives now include estimating the biomass of anchovy and sardine, hydrographic characterization, acoustic registrations, and the distribution and abundance of microplastics, zooplankton, seabirds, mammals, and various species using environmental DNA. These data support fish stock and ecosystem-based assessments and management.

**Content**
Data on the quantities of marine litter (specifically microplastics) sampled during the BIOMAN campaigns for the period between 2017 and 2013. The microplastic data are provided by station, both in terms of the number of items and weight.

**DOI**
This data repository is archived on Zenodo as pat of LAMARCA_TOOL.LAMACA_TOOL has the following DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.14002078

